1. **A wellhead adaptor assembly** for controlling flow of hydrocarbons from a wellbore, the wellhead adaptor assembly comprising:

   a wellhead adaptor body having a main flow passage extending therethrough and configured for fluid communication with the wellbore;

   a drilling valve disposed in the main flow passage, the drilling valve being biased or otherwise configured to remain in a normally open condition during drilling operations;

   a side branch extending from the wellhead adaptor body and being in selective fluid communication with the main flow passage, the side branch being connectable to a hydrocarbon storage vessel or storage line;

   a production branch extending from the wellhead adaptor body and being in selective fluid communication with the main flow passage, the production branch being connectable to a production flow line;

   at least one branch valve positioned to control hydrocarbon flow through the side branch;

   at least one production valve positioned to control hydrocarbon flow through the production branch;

   one or more sensors arranged to detect a hydrocarbon flow condition in the wellhead adaptor assembly, the hydrocarbon flow condition including at least one of flow rate, pressure, hydrocarbon concentration, or fluid composition; and

   a controller operatively coupled to the one or more sensors, the branch valve, and the production valve,

   wherein the controller is configured to compare the detected hydrocarbon flow condition with one or more preset threshold values and, in response thereto, selectively open or close at least one of the branch valve and the production valve to direct hydrocarbon flow selectively to the storage vessel or to the production flow line.

2. **The wellhead adaptor assembly of claim 1**, wherein the controller is configured to open the branch valve when the detected hydrocarbon flow condition exceeds a first preset threshold value, thereby diverting hydrocarbons through the side branch to storage.

3. **The wellhead adaptor assembly of claim 1**, wherein the controller is configured to close the branch valve when the detected hydrocarbon flow condition falls below a second preset threshold value.

4. **The wellhead adaptor assembly of claim 1**, wherein the controller is configured to open the production valve when the detected hydrocarbon flow condition is within a preset production range.

5. **The wellhead adaptor assembly of claim 1**, wherein the drilling valve remains open unless manually or automatically actuated to isolate the wellbore.

6. **The wellhead adaptor assembly of claim 1**, wherein the one or more sensors comprise at least one flow meter positioned upstream of the side branch and production branch.

7. **The wellhead adaptor assembly of claim 1**, wherein the one or more sensors comprise a pressure sensor arranged to detect pressure in the main flow passage.

8. **The wellhead adaptor assembly of claim 1**, wherein the preset threshold values include a minimum hydrocarbon flow threshold for initiating diversion to storage and a maximum hydrocarbon flow threshold for shutting or restricting flow through at least one branch.

9. **The wellhead adaptor assembly of claim 1**, wherein the controller is configured to actuate the branch valve and the production valve independently.

10. **The wellhead adaptor assembly of claim 1**, wherein the side branch and the production branch are arranged downstream of the normally open drilling valve.
